  "body": "In the example of **4.13.1.2 Creating a customized built-in element** in https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/scripting.html#custom-elements, we define a customized built-in element named _plastic-button_.\n\n``` javascript\nclass PlasticButton extends HTMLButtonElement {\n  constructor() {\n    super();\n  }\n}\n\ncustomElements.define(\"plastic-button\", PlasticButton, { extends: \"button\" });\n```\n\nThen we can use constructor to create a type-extended element.\n\n``` javascript\nconst plasticButton = new PlasticButton();\n```\n\nSince [HTMLButtonElement doesn't have constructor](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/forms.html#htmlbuttonelement), does it mean the super() call in PlasticButton's constructor will actually run the [HTMLElement's constructor step](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/dom.html#dom-htmlelement)?\n",
